    <string name="section_beta">BETA</string>
    <string name="row_island">Super Island</string>
    <string name="hint_island_beta">Beta, Xiaomi only. While you record, the island shows a small icon and the timer; a tap on it gives pause and stop. HyperOS hides the island whenever the status bar is pulled down, so the notification there carries the same buttons. Shizuku is needed once to grant the permission.</string>
    <string name="island_value_off">Off · beta</string>
    <string name="island_value_on">On · beta</string>
    <string name="island_value_need">Needs Shizuku</string>
    <string name="island_title">Super Island (beta)</string>
    <string name="island_body">HyperOS can show the recording in its Super Island: a small icon and the timer. Tap the island for pause and stop. HyperOS hides the island on its own as soon as the status bar is pulled down, and the notification there has the same buttons. That permission can only be given through Shizuku.</string>
    <string name="island_body_on">While you record, the island shows a small icon and the timer; a tap gives pause and stop. HyperOS hides it by itself whenever the status bar is pulled down. Choose Hidden if you would rather have no island at all; the notification stays either way.</string>
    <string name="island_enable">Enable with Shizuku</string>
    <string name="island_disable">Turn off</string>
    <string name="island_need_shizuku_title">Shizuku is needed</string>
    <string name="island_need_shizuku_body">Super Island is beta and only works on Xiaomi phones. Android does not let a normal app ask for the island permission, so DenRecorder needs Shizuku once. Install Shizuku, start it (wireless debugging or root), then come back here.</string>
    <string name="island_install_shizuku">Get Shizuku</string>
    <string name="island_waiting_shizuku">Shizuku is installed but not running. Open it and start the service, then tap Enable again.</string>
    <string name="island_open_shizuku">Open Shizuku</string>
    <string name="island_allow_in_shizuku">Allow DenRecorder in Shizuku\'s dialog</string>
    <string name="island_granting">Granting the island permission…</string>
    <string name="island_done_title">Super Island is on</string>
    <string name="island_done_body">A small test entry should appear in the island now. If it does not, this HyperOS build keeps the island for system apps; the recording notification still works as before.</string>
    <string name="island_failed_title">The island permission was not granted</string>
    <string name="island_failed_body">SystemUI still does not let DenRecorder draw in the island. On many builds only root can grant this. Shizuku said: %1$s</string>
    <string name="island_denied_body">Shizuku did not allow DenRecorder. Tap Enable again and choose Allow in Shizuku\'s dialog.</string>
    <string name="island_request_again">Try again</string>
